{% comment %}
  Appx — Product Specs Table
  Storefront app block. Renders the spec table assigned to the current product.

  - Resolves the assigned template metaobject `spec` in TWO tiers (feature 43,
    data-model §9); the disjoint ACTIVE set guarantees <=1 table per product:
      1. The shop routing map: `snippets/spec-table-resolve.liquid` reads
         `shop.metafields["$app"].routing.value` and emits the matched template
         HANDLE (or nothing, incl. when the product is in `excludedProductGids`);
         the handle resolves to the metaobject via
         `metaobjects["$app:appx_spec_table"][handle]` (raw-handle lookup, proven
         live — data-model §9). Explicit single-product assignments arrive the
         same way, as `routing.byProduct` entries.
      2. No match -> `spec` stays blank -> nothing renders.
    🚫 There was a tier ahead of these: the per-product `metaobject_reference`
    metafield `product.metafields["$app"].spec_table.value` (features 34/35),
    REMOVED 2026-08-04 along with its definition. No app code ever wrote it, so
    it could only ever be set by hand in Admin. Do not reinstate the read without
    reinstating the definition in `shopify.app.toml` — a metafield with no
    definition resolves to nil and the branch would be silently dead.
  - `.status`/`.rows` are read as `.status.value` / `.rows.value` (json -> array).
  - SECTION_HEADER rows span both columns; DATA rows are label/value pairs.
  - Value cells (all part types, incl. SHOPIFY_FIELD / METAFIELD resolution
    against the live product) render via `snippets/spec-table-value.liquid` —
    see that file + `context/features/35-storefront-value-part-resolution.md`.
  - `hideWhenEmpty` is a WHOLE-CELL character test (locked decision, slice 2):
    the row is skipped when the flag is set and the fully resolved cell has
    zero non-whitespace characters. `strip_html` drops the `<br>`s first so
    LINE_BREAKs never count as content. TEXT-only cells always render.
  - Author-entered text is escaped inside the snippet (merchants author these —
    never inject raw HTML); the captured cell is emitted unfiltered because it
    is already escaped and may legitimately contain `<br>`.
  - Silent by design: a non-ACTIVE status, no assigned template, or no rows
    renders NOTHING on the storefront (no diagnostic text, no empty box).
  - CONTENT-FREE TABLES render nothing either (feature 74). Two render-time
    gates, mirrored exactly in the admin preview renderer:
      R1 a SECTION_HEADER whose label is blank after `strip` is skipped — the
         element exists only to carry a title, and an empty one paints a bare
         grey band (the BANDED default) with nothing in it.
      R2 if NO row survives its gate, no wrapper is emitted at all — not an
         empty <div class="appx-spec-table">, not an empty <table>. This is
         what makes the "silent by design" line above true for a rows array
         that is non-empty but resolves to nothing (e.g. the editor's starter
         scaffold: one blank section header + five empty hideWhenEmpty rows).
    R2 is why the body is built into `table_body` via `capture` FIRST and the
    wrapper decided after: the <div> used to open before the loop, and a data
    cell's emptiness is undecidable without rendering it against the live
    product. One pass, no double-render. NOT gated: a section header with a
    real label whose rows are all hidden still renders (authored content —
    see feature 74 "R3", deliberately out of scope).

  CSS lives in assets/spec-table.css and is loaded via the schema "stylesheet"
  attribute — theme app extension blocks cannot use the {% stylesheet %} tag.
{% endcomment %}

{%- comment -%}
  Tier 1 — shop routing map. Resolve a template handle from the product's
  attributes, then look up its metaobject by handle. The resolver emits nothing for
  an excluded / unmatched product, so `spec` stays blank and nothing renders
  (tier 2).
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  assign routing = shop.metafields["$app"].routing.value
-%}
{%- capture routed_handle -%}{%- render "spec-table-resolve", product: product, routing: routing -%}{%- endcapture -%}
{%- comment -%}
  Shopify wraps app-extension snippet output in `<!-- BEGIN/END app snippet -->`
  comments; strip_html removes those (and any stray tags) so only the plain
  handle slug remains, then strip trims whitespace. A metaobject handle has no
  HTML characters, so strip_html is lossless here.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- assign routed_handle = routed_handle | strip_html | strip -%}
{%- if routed_handle != blank -%}
  {%- assign spec = metaobjects["$app:appx_spec_table"][routed_handle] -%}
{%- endif -%}
{%- liquid
  assign rows = spec.rows.value
  assign styling_css = spec.styling_css.value
  assign styling = spec.styling.value
-%}

{%- comment -%}
  Collapsible sections (feature 57 Step 9a). These two knobs are the ONLY ones
  Liquid reads from the raw `styling` field rather than the precomputed
  `styling_css`, and deliberately so: they are MARKUP decisions (`<details>` and
  its `open` attribute), not part of the CSS mapping, so Step 7's "the server
  precomputes; Liquid only prints" rule is not violated — there is no per-knob
  table here to fall out of sync, just two scalars.

  The wire shape is OVERRIDES-ONLY, which is what makes this free of defaulting
  logic: a default-styled template has no `sectionsCollapsible` key at all, so
  the lookup is nil, so it is falsy — the correct default (false) with zero code.
  Same for the initial state via `| default:`.

  ⚠️ THAT `| default:` MUST TRACK `DEFAULT_SECTIONS_INITIAL_STATE` in
  app/utils/tableStyling.ts. A mismatch is SILENT — the admin preview and the
  storefront would simply disagree about which sections start open, on exactly
  the templates that store no value (i.e. most of them). Changed ALL_OPEN →
  FIRST_OPEN with the domain default on 2026-07-30.

  It is enforced, despite Liquid being outside the module graph:
  `specTableLiquidDefaultsContract.test.ts` reads this file off disk and
  compares the literal below to the domain constant. Change one, and the suite
  names the other.

  Collapsible degrades to the flat shape when the template has no section
  headers (nothing to collapse), matching the admin preview renderer exactly —
  see app/routes/app.templates_.$id/specTablePreviewHtml.ts.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  assign section_rows = rows | where: "rowType", "SECTION_HEADER"
  assign collapsible = false
  if styling.sectionsCollapsible and section_rows.size > 0
    assign collapsible = true
  endif
  assign initial_state = styling.sectionsInitialState | default: "FIRST_OPEN"
-%}

{%- comment -%}
  Styling (feature 57 Step 7). `styling_css` is PRECOMPUTED server-side at sync
  time — `.classes` is the space-joined BEM modifier list for the wrapper,
  `.vars` the `--appx-spec-*: v;` declarations — so this template performs NO
  styling logic and needs no change when a knob is added. The mapping lives once,
  in `app/utils/tableStylingCss.ts`, shared with the admin preview (data-model §10).

  An entry synced before this field existed leaves both blank, which renders
  exactly as it did pre-Step-7 (lazy backfill; self-heals on the next save).

  `escape` is defense in depth only: values are whitelist-validated upstream at
  `parseStylingValues` (hex-only colors, clamped integers, list-checked keywords),
  and the output contains no quotes or angle brackets, so it is a no-op here.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- if spec != blank and spec.status.value == "ACTIVE" and rows != blank and rows.size > 0 -%}
  {%- comment -%}
    Feature 74 — R2. The body is CAPTURED, then the wrapper is emitted only if
    something actually rendered. `has_content` is assigned inside the capture and
    read after it: `capture` redirects OUTPUT, not assignments, so the flag (like
    `table_open` / `details_open` / `section_index` below) is template-scoped and
    survives the block.

    The capture is the whole reason this works in one pass. A DATA row's
    emptiness depends on the live product (`spec-table-value` resolves
    SHOPIFY_FIELD / METAFIELD parts), so a pre-pass "will anything render?" would
    have to render every value cell twice.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- assign has_content = false -%}
  {%- capture table_body -%}
    {%- comment -%}
      TWO markup shapes, switched by `collapsible`, sharing ONE row loop so the
      hideWhenEmpty gate can never differ between them:

      - OFF (the default): one <table>, section headers as full-width <tr>. Byte
        for byte what shipped before Step 9a — every existing template renders
        through here and must not move.
      - ON: one <details> per section header, each wrapping its OWN <table>.
        Rows appearing BEFORE the first section header render in a leading bare
        <table> with no <details> (there is no section to name), so `table_open`
        opens lazily. A section whose rows are all hidden renders as an empty
        collapsible — no new emptiness logic, which would change the OFF path
        too. Each per-section table carries an aria-label with the section
        title, because the split costs it the <th scope="colgroup"> heading.

      No JavaScript: <details> is native, keyboard-operable, and announces its
      own expanded state.

      EXPLICIT ARIA ROLES (feature 70) restate semantics this markup already
      expresses correctly via the tags + scope attributes. They are here because
      the STACKED layouts apply `display: block` (spec-table.css), which drops an
      element out of the CSS table model and takes the browser's implicit table
      semantics with it — a screen reader stops announcing label/value as a
      header/cell pair. ARIA roles are immune to `display`, so they survive it.

      They are UNCONDITIONAL on purpose. The mobile stacked rule is a MEDIA
      QUERY, and Liquid renders server-side with no idea how wide the shopper's
      screen is — so a role emitted only when `rowLayout == STACKED` would leave
      every narrow-screen shopper of every two-column template broken. In
      two-column mode these roles are harmless restatements of what the tags
      already mean.

      ALL OR NOTHING: table -> rowgroup -> row -> rowheader/cell must stay
      complete. A `role="row"` with no table role above it can be dropped
      outright by assistive tech, children included — a partial chain is worse
      than none. `specTableAriaContract.test.ts` fails if one goes missing.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    {%- if collapsible -%}
      {%- assign table_open = false -%}
    {%- else -%}
      <table class="appx-spec-table__table" role="table"><tbody role="rowgroup">
      {%- assign table_open = true -%}
    {%- endif -%}
    {%- assign details_open = false -%}
    {%- assign section_index = 0 -%}
    {%- comment -%}
      Shopify caps for-loops at 50 iterations; templates hold up to
      MAX_TEMPLATE_ROWS (200) rows, so iterate in 50-row chunks.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    {%- assign row_chunks = rows.size | plus: 49 | divided_by: 50 -%}
    {%- for chunk in (1..row_chunks) -%}
      {%- assign row_offset = chunk | minus: 1 | times: 50 -%}
      {%- for row in rows offset: row_offset limit: 50 -%}
        {%- if row.rowType == "SECTION_HEADER" -%}
          {%- comment -%}
            R1 (feature 74). A section header carries nothing but its title, so a
            blank one is skipped in BOTH shapes. Tested trimmed, emitted untrimmed
            — the same test-input/output split `hideWhenEmpty` already uses. The
            filter has to land in an `assign`: Liquid `if` conditions do not
            accept filters.
          {%- endcomment -%}
          {%- assign section_label = row.label | strip -%}
          {%- if collapsible -%}
            {%- comment -%}
              A blank header still CLOSES the open group before vanishing. Without
              the close, the rows that followed it would be filed under the
              PREVIOUS section's heading — a worse bug than the band it removes.
              They instead hit the lazy-open branch below and land in a fresh bare
              unnamed table, exactly as rows before the first section header do.
              `section_index` is deliberately NOT incremented: a skipped section is
              not a section, so FIRST_OPEN still opens the first REAL one.
            {%- endcomment -%}
            {%- if table_open -%}</tbody></table>{%- assign table_open = false -%}{%- endif -%}
            {%- if details_open -%}</details>{%- assign details_open = false -%}{%- endif -%}
            {%- if section_label != blank -%}
              {%- liquid
                assign is_open = false
                if initial_state == "ALL_OPEN"
                  assign is_open = true
                elsif initial_state == "FIRST_OPEN" and section_index == 0
                  assign is_open = true
                endif
              -%}
              <details class="appx-spec-table__section-group"{% if is_open %} open{% endif %}>
                <summary class="appx-spec-table__section-summary">{{ row.label | escape }}</summary>
                <table class="appx-spec-table__table" role="table" aria-label="{{ row.label | escape }}"><tbody role="rowgroup">
              {%- liquid
                assign details_open = true
                assign table_open = true
                assign section_index = section_index | plus: 1
                assign has_content = true
              -%}
            {%- endif -%}
          {%- else -%}
            {%- if section_label != blank -%}
              <tr class="appx-spec-table__section-row" role="row">
                <th class="appx-spec-table__section" colspan="2" scope="colgroup" role="columnheader" aria-colspan="2">{{ row.label | escape }}</th>
              </tr>
              {%- assign has_content = true -%}
            {%- endif -%}
          {%- endif -%}
        {%- else -%}
          {%- capture cell -%}{% render "spec-table-value", row: row, product: product %}{%- endcapture -%}
          {%- assign cell_plain = cell | strip_html | strip -%}
          {%- unless row.hideWhenEmpty and cell_plain == blank -%}
            {%- unless table_open -%}
              <table class="appx-spec-table__table" role="table"><tbody role="rowgroup">
              {%- assign table_open = true -%}
            {%- endunless -%}
            <tr class="appx-spec-table__row" role="row">
              <th class="appx-spec-table__label" scope="row" role="rowheader">{{ row.label | escape }}</th>
              <td class="appx-spec-table__value" role="cell">{{ cell }}</td>
            </tr>
            {%- assign has_content = true -%}
          {%- endunless -%}
        {%- endif -%}
      {%- endfor -%}
    {%- endfor -%}
    {%- if table_open -%}</tbody></table>{%- endif -%}
    {%- if details_open -%}</details>{%- endif -%}
  {%- endcapture -%}
  {%- comment -%}
    `table_body` is printed RAW: Liquid does not auto-escape, and every
    author-entered string inside it was escaped at emission time (same posture as
    `{{ cell }}` above). When nothing rendered, the captured body — which may
    still hold an empty <table><tbody></tbody></table> from the flat shape's
    eager open — is simply discarded.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- if has_content -%}
    <div class="appx-spec-table {{ styling_css.classes | escape }}" style="{{ styling_css.vars | escape }}" {{ block.shopify_attributes }}>{{ table_body }}</div>
  {%- endif -%}
{%- endif -%}

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Product specs table",
  "target": "section",
  "stylesheet": "spec-table.css",
  "enabled_on": {
    "templates": ["product"]
  },
  "settings": []
}
{% endschema %}
